# sweep: skip
# The sheet is owed only when whats-new.txt is for the running version, and
# between releases it is for the next one. The sweep cannot hand one route an
# environment variable, so this route is run by hand, with the version the
# file names standing in for the running one. --bare leaves out the sweep's
# seed, which marks the notes as read for every other launcher route:
#
#   KOBO_LAUNCHER_NOTES_VERSION=0.3.42 python3 scripts/check-apps-sim.py launcher \
#     --bare --route examples/launcher/drive-whats-new.kobo --out target/sim-check-whats-new
#
# The version and the leads below are this release's. Rewrite them with the
# file.
wait-for What's new in Cobalt 0.3.42
expect Warmth:
expect Home and away:
expect Update notes:
shot whats-new
# One tap puts it away, and the grid under it is where it was.
tap Done
wait-idle
expect-missing What's new in Cobalt
expect-missing Warmth:
expect-missing Home and away:
expect-missing Update notes:
expect-missing Done
expect Cobalt
expect App Store
shot whats-new-put-away
# Putting it away was written down, so a new start does not show it again.
restart
wait-for Cobalt
wait-idle
expect-missing What's new in Cobalt
expect-missing Done
expect App Store
tap-id next
wait-for 2 of
